.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-server-console - Open a one-time VNC console ticket


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server console  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a one-time VNC console ticket

.PP
Returns a websocket URL and password valid for about a minute. Never send an Idempotency-Key here (400). In tr-ist-1 the ticket is a WebMKS websocket (\fBprotocol: webmks\fR, empty password: the URL is the one-time secret). tr-ist-1: the WebSocket URL is on konsol.gyrohosting.com (single-use ticket).

.PP
API: POST /cloud/servers/{id}/console (operationId openConsole, scope cloud_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for console

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait until the server is no longer busy

.PP
\fB--wait-timeout\fP=15m0s
	maximum time for --wait


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
